.TH CHECK@COURSE_NUM@ 1

.SH NAME
check@COURSE_NUM@ \- check Java source code style

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B check@COURSE_NUM@ [\fIOPTION\fP...] \fIFILE\fP...

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBcheck@COURSE_NUM@\fP script verifies that the specified source code FILEs adhere
to the guidelines in the \fBCSCI @COURSE_NUM@ Code Style Guide\fP (@GUIDE_URL@).
The script uses Checkstyle (https://checkstyle.org/) to automate
the process of checking the Java code in each FILE. Each FILE may be a path to
a \fI.java\fP file or a path to a directory.

The script runs Checkstyle configured with the CSCI @COURSE_NUM@ rules,
filters verbose package namespace prefixes from violation reports, and automatically
opens the style guide in a web browser if violations are detected and the
\fBBROWSER\fP environment variable is defined.

.SH EXAMPLES
To check a single Java source code file, say
\fIsrc/cs@COURSE_NUM@/util/Example.java\fP, use:
.PP
.nf
.RS
$ \fBcheck@COURSE_NUM@\fP src/cs@COURSE_NUM@/util/Example.java
.RE
.fi
.PP
To check all Java source code files under a directory, say
\fIsrc\fP, use:
.PP
.nf
.RS
$ \fBcheck@COURSE_NUM@\fP src
.RE
.fi
.PP
When a guideline violation is found, the output may contain one or more lines
that look like this:
.PP
.nf
.RS
[ERROR] src/cs@COURSE_NUM@/util/Example.java:2: Missing a Javadoc comment. [MissingJavadocType]
.RE
.fi
.PP
In the last example, MissingJavadocType is the name of the specific guideline in the
\fBCSCI @COURSE_NUM@ Code Style Guide\fP (@GUIDE_URL@) that was violated on line 2
of \fIsrc/cs@COURSE_NUM@/util/Example.java\fP.

.SH OPTIONS
Any standard \fBcheckstyle\fP(1) options may be passed to \fBcheck@COURSE_NUM@\fP,
with the exception of \fB-c\fP (which is reserved and disallows overriding the
course style checks configuration).
.PP
Common options include:

.TP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP
Show the Checkstyle help message and exit.

.TP
\fB-V\fP, \fB--version\fP
Print Checkstyle version information and exit.

.TP
\fB-f\fP=\fIformat\fP
Specifies the output format (\fBplain\fP, \fBxml\fP, or \fBsarif\fP). Defaults to \fBplain\fP.

.TP
\fB-o\fP=\fIoutputPath\fP
Sets the output file for violation reports (defaults to standard output).

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBCS@COURSE_NUM@_CHECKS\fP
Path to the style checks XML configuration file. Defaults to
\fI@CHECKS_FILE_PATH@\fP.

.TP
\fBBROWSER\fP
The path or name of the web browser executable used to open the style guide
at \fI@GUIDE_URL@\fP when violations are encountered.

.SH FILES
.TP
\fI@CHECKS_FILE_PATH@\fP
The Checkstyle XML rules configuration file for CSCI @COURSE_NUM@.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fP
All specified Java source code files comply with the style guide.
.TP
\fB>0\fP
Style guide violations were detected or an error occurred during execution.

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcheckstyle\fP(1)

